From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:38:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] docs(acnh): the picture shape's lower bound is the game's
 1.25

Headless on a Mac at 3.0.3 main: 1.25 and 1.3 start, 1.245 crashes at
boot in the actor manager's layout lookup (a null from main+0x7a1ba0
written through at main+0x1961090). The threshold follows the display
size (bits 4 and 7 of DM_SCREEN_ASPECT_SITES), not the layout size
(bit 1 alone is harmless), so a standing phone's 0.92 picture does not
start; 2.167 runs. The game note says so, and that 1.25 is the tallest
picture that starts.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the note said the 0.92 crash had no stack; headless on a Mac at 3.0.3
main it does: the game refuses a display taller than 1536 (layout 1024), where
the actor manager's layout lookup returns null, so a standing phone's 0.92
picture does not start and 1.25 is the tallest that does; 2.167 runs.
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the picture shape

---
 dm/games/01006F8002326000/README.md | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/01006F8002326000/README.md b/dm/games/01006F8002326000/README.md
index 92739bd3..5361ab0d 100644
--- a/dm/games/01006F8002326000/README.md
+++ b/dm/games/01006F8002326000/README.md
@@ -63,6 +63,8 @@ Checked on a Mac (M1, macOS 27, headless, an island save) against 16:9: the 3D v
 
 A phone standing up shows the game's picture in the upper half of the window and the companion band in the lower half: `dm/ios/Sources/DmLayout.h` splits the window at its midpoint, and the picture is fitted into that half. *Picture shape* `auto` asks for the half's own shape (twice the screen's width / its height: 0.92 on a 19.5:9 phone, 1.12 on a 375x667 one, 1.39 on an iPad; an iPhone shows the game full screen, so the screen and the window agree), so the fitted picture fills the half exactly: its background covers the area with nothing cropped and nothing stretched. The game's own layouts keep 16:9, centred in the picture (the adapter's `SetProjectionMtx` y-row division, below), so its HUD and menus are not stretched either; the touch screen maps a touch on the taller picture back onto that centred rectangle (`ui_y` in `hle_touch.c`), so a control is hit where it is drawn. A manual `DM_SCREEN_ASPECT` that does not match the half keeps its whole picture and leaves bars instead of cropping it. The picture never takes more than half the window, so the band keeps the other half.
 
+**0.92 does not start yet**: the game refuses a display taller than 1536 ([Adaptive view consistency](#adaptive-view-consistency-current)), so a standing phone asking for its half's own shape crashes at boot before the first present. The tallest picture that starts is 1.25, which leaves bars above and below in the half.
+
 **`auto` is resolved once, at the game's start**, because `DM_SCREEN_ASPECT` is written into the frame step state page and the game builds its window textures from it. A game started in portrait keeps its 0.92 picture after the phone turns to landscape (pillarboxed at the sides); to get the wider picture of [Screen shape](#screen-shape-dm_screen_aspect-current) on a 19.5:9 phone, start in landscape. Turning a landscape game to portrait keeps the wide picture, fitted into the upper half.
 
 **A phone standing up is handheld, so the game's own keyboard takes touches.** The profile sets no `op_mode`, so the game starts docked and the host hands it no touch points (`touch_read` in `hle_hid.c`), which leaves the game's keyboard unreachable. The front end therefore switches the console mode by the screen's orientation while no TV shows the picture (`followOrientation` in `front_ios.m`): standing up it goes handheld and lying down it returns to the mode the player had, a choice made in the in-game menu included. The game reads touches in both modes, so nothing else has to change, and the switch is the console mode change notification the game watches, so it follows while it runs. Handheld also renders at 1280x720, so the picture is the handheld one while the phone stands up. *Console mode* in the in-game menu (or `DM_OPMODE=0` in `Documents/env.txt`) still works for a phone lying down.
@@ -87,7 +89,7 @@ On a taller picture the game caches projections and screen rectangles that a cha
 
 `main+0x265140` is the single `ret` of `nn::ui2d::DrawInfo::SetProjectionMtx`. One chained stub runs the upstream y-row division first (its 16:9 test reads m0 and m5, which the adapter's `Lscreen_projection` rewrites), then calls the adapter's keyboard dock; the adapter adds its offset to index 6 instead of overwriting it. `main+0x27d4c0` forces the footer subtree dirty at `Pane::Calculate` entry and `main+0x27d570` runs `duo_calc` after `CalculateGlobalMatrix`: the two were disassembled and coexist.
 
-The adapter follows the host's `DM_SCREEN_ASPECT` through `dm_fps_state +0x58`. It was built and checked for 1.3 to 1.77; a phone standing up now asks for its upper half's shape, 0.92 on a 19.5:9 phone and 1.12 on a 375x667 one, below that range, and no device has confirmed those two ratios yet (an earlier report of a crash at 0.92 has no stack or cause). An iPad's 1.39 and a 4:3 one's 1.5 stay inside it. It does not support arbitrary ratios or folding-display rotation. At `+0x58 = 0` (16:9) every adapter stub runs the original instructions.
+The adapter follows the host's `DM_SCREEN_ASPECT` through `dm_fps_state +0x58`. **Its lower bound is the game's, at 1.25**: a picture shorter than that (a display height over 1536, a layout height over 1024) crashes at boot. The actor manager's layout lookup returns null and the caller writes through it (`main+0x7a1ba0` → `main+0x1961090`, fault address 0x8). Headless on a Mac at 3.0.3 `main`, 1.25 and 1.3 start and run, 1.245 does not, and the threshold is the display size's: with only bits 4 and 7 of `DM_SCREEN_ASPECT_SITES` on it still crashes, while the layout size alone (bit 1) is harmless. Above 16:9 the range is open: 2.167 (a 19.5:9 phone lying down) ran 120 s headless. A phone standing up therefore cannot ask for its upper half's shape (0.92) yet: 1.25 is the tallest picture the game starts with. An iPad's 1.39 and a 4:3 one's 1.5 stay inside the range. It does not support arbitrary ratios or folding-display rotation. At `+0x58 = 0` (16:9) every adapter stub runs the original instructions.
 
 The frame stamps are values in the free part of the state page, with no host pointer: `+0xa8` is the host's present counter (`dm_guest_frame_tick`, `hle_os.c`, one relaxed store each present), `+0xb0` the keyboard frame's stamp and `+0xb8` a touch panel's, written by `keyboard_frame` and `touch_page` through `Ltouch_stamp` (`x17` = 8 and 16). `Lrecent_keyboard` subtracts the first two, so "the inline keyboard rendered in the last two presents" needs no host state. `keyboard_window` keeps its own stamp at `+0x38`, which nothing reads: AnimalDuo's touch-context (bit 3) was not ported.
 
